    "q-217248": {
      "dom_id": "step-q217248",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Suppose that $y$ varies inversely with $x$ and that $y=\\frac{3}{4}$ when $x=12.$ Then, if $x=\\frac{1}{3},$ $y=${{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "Since $y$ varies inversely with $x,$ we use the equation\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{k}{x}.\n$$\n\nWe are told that $y=\\frac{3}{4}$ when $x=12.$ We substitute this data into the equation to find $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4} & =\\frac{k}{12} \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}\\cdot 12 & =k \\\\ 9 & =k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the inverse variation is given by \n\n$$\ny=\\frac{9}{x}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the value of $x=\\frac{1}{3}$ into this equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{9}{(\\frac{1}{3})} \\\\  & =9÷(\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =9\\cdot (\\frac{3}{1}) \\\\  & =27.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
